                        "documentation": " Run diff on strings {a} and {b}. Any indices returned by this function,\n either directly or via callback arguments, are 1-based.\n\n Examples:\n\n ```lua\n vim.text.diff('a\\n', 'b\\nc\\n')\n -- =>\n -- @@ -1 +1,2 @@\n -- -a\n -- +b\n -- +c\n\n vim.text.diff('a\\n', 'b\\nc\\n', {result_type = 'indices'})\n -- =>\n -- {\n --   {1, 1, 1, 2}\n -- }\n ```\n\n@*param* `a` — First string to compare\n\n@*param* `b` — Second string to compare\n\n@*return* — See {opts.result_type}. `nil` if {opts.on_hunk} is given.",
